+# Plan: JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+## Constitution Check
+- I: RFC 6902 §4–§5 and RFC 6901 §3–§4 named in spec; rules implemented exactly (move-prefix error, test
+  equality, atomicity, `-`, `null` vs missing).
+- II: no dependencies. III: tests first (`test/patch.test.ts`), seen failing. IV: work on a deep clone, never
+  mutate input; own-key-only access; keys set with `defineProperty`. V: strict TS, exported + documented,
+  `.js`/`.ts` import style as existing. VI: single function plus small helpers in `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Design
+- Refactor pointer parsing into internal `parsePointer(pointer): string[]` reused by `resolvePointer`.
+- `applyPatch`: validate patch shape, deep-clone document (own clone helper, JSON values only), apply ops
+  sequentially to the clone with helpers `getAt`, `addAt`, `removeAt`; clone `value`s on insert.
+- Root-level replacement returns the new root; JSON pointer errors are rethrown as `JsonPatchError`.
+- Update README.
